title Caravan amend -- a settlement an operator already read is corrected where they read it
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; condense REMEMBER when a set closes; send each finished increment
think Read context/KYRI.md and context/RADIANT_STYLE.md before anything else, so the voice shaped the round from the first token rather than being applied to it afterward.
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md end to end: every living row reads CLOSED or Released, %96 and %97 both closed on the lap before this one. No agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue is open rather than blocked.
think Read the running thread the way the seed asks -- the top rows of session-logs/README.md and the newest log's recommend line. The recant rung named its own successor plainly: what a plan owes an operator who already acted on a judgment since taken back, since a reversal arriving after the report was read has no way yet to reach the person who read it.
think Read the whole of caravan/recant.rye before writing a line -- the shapes, the notes, the supervisor, the mend, the settlement, the lap, the self-test. A rung of this arc is built by carrying the one below it whole and adding exactly one question, so the elder rung is the specification.
think Named the rung under the Comlink tendency -- clearest, warmest, safest word. **Amend** is plain, warm to type, and collides with nothing seated in the tree; the one prior hit is an unrelated equinox witness filename.
think Found the honest gap. The wire is truthful the whole time: recant publishes its reversal, moves the settlement from `borne` to `carried`, and every note says what is so. What no rung below reaches is the person who read the elder word and went home. The measurement had to weigh a record against its READER rather than against itself.
think Shaped the rung SLC -- one scope, honestly bounded. A plan-level `notice` word beside the review; a standing reading that survives the run as the appraisal does, for a plainer reason (a reader's copy survives whatever the wire does); an amendment written in an operator's own words rather than one glyph per phase, since it is the first note of this arc addressed to a person.
think Rebased the module one tier out mechanically first -- report accessors gain an `inner`, the rung below becomes recant, the recantation section becomes delegations -- and let the compiler find the two shadowed names rather than reasoning about them.
think Proved six RED paths on metal BEFORE claiming anything. Withhold the amendment; leave the answered reading standing; disarm the moment; disarm the supply; let the count stop closing; and plant a correction addressed to a reading the wire never named, which the armed supply guard refuses at the run.
obs The council rota doc this lap was item 16, Simple Lovable Complete. Its three questions governed the scope directly: one clear question honestly bounded, a rung a person would genuinely want (an operator finally hears that the word they carried away has changed), and a loop that closes fully -- fold, wire, four refusals, measurement, and the generalization test one tier out.
obs The finding parts from every rung before it on price. Nine rungs of this arc each cost something to be honest -- one more dependent, a repair re-run, a judgment taken back. This one costs NOTHING: both runs spend the same six dependents, repair the same three arcs, and settle the same word. A correction costs only the willingness to say so, and that is the whole moral of the rung.
obs The supply refusal `AmendUnread` is defense in depth over its own fold, exactly as `RecantUnappraised` is below it. Proving its RED needed a planted control that both nulls the reading the run reads back and means to correct somebody anyway -- named honestly rather than left as decoration nobody had watched fire.
obs Chose `on_the_wire` over `standing` for the refusal's count parameter after the compiler named a shadow: `standing` is already the supervisor's own reach into the closed record, and one word meaning two things inside one module is a red waiting to be written.
loom witness=caravan_amend_witness phases=6 dependents_silent=6 dependents_posted=6 absorbed=3 lost=3 reseated=3 recanted=1 amended_silent=0 amended_posted=1 superseded_unposted_silent=1 superseded_unposted_posted=0 pairs=16 red_paths_proven=6
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=60 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=true
loom module=caravan_amend lines=3725 asserts=219 usize=0
file caravan/amend.rye the rung -- a settlement an operator already read corrected where they read it, carrying recant whole beneath it
file tools/caravan_amend_witness.rish the witness -- reads every note off the wire outside the run that wrote it, as an operator would
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the new rung in the choir, which sings 60 from a cold tree
file caravan/README.md the rung's durable entry, so the record outlives this log
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge and the git nib, in the same commit as the work
recommend keep-going the arc has answered for reach at every moment of a dependent's life, repaired what a fall cost, learned which losses to leave alone, weighed the losses nobody spoke to, taken back its own stale judgments, and now writes to the reader those judgments misled -- so the question standing above it is what a plan owes a reader it cannot name: the amendment waits on the wire for somebody to come back and read it, which is no correction at all for an operator who never returns, and asks whether a record should ever reach outward rather than only publish.
